data.format:
One greyscale JPG per page, downscaled from the archive's scan to 1376×2000 px (about 0.7 MB each). The file name is the image identifier of the archive's IIIF image service (`sta_h_43_36_0363` is image 363 of the volume). The ground truth is one JSON file per page, following the `AddressBookPage` dataclass in `dataclass.py`, with one `[x0, y0, x1, y1]` box per entry in pixel coordinates of the downscaled image, (x0, y0) the top-left and (x1, y1) the bottom-right corner, in reading order (column by column, top to bottom):

The first two entries of `sta_h_43_36_0363`:

```json
{
  "entries": [
    {"box": [226, 254, 745, 344]},
    {"box": [224, 341, 745, 401]}
  ]
}
```

The 64 pages hold 5,494 entries, between 38 and 105 per page (median 88). An entry that runs over several printed lines has one box covering all of them. A cross-reference standing in place of entries, such as "(Siehe Konditoren.)" under a trade heading, is boxed as an entry (about 46 of them); trade headings and sub-headings, notes under a heading, legends of marks, footnotes, running heads and page numbers are not boxed.
